"""Suzuki 2017 RM-Z250 and 2022 RM85 wiring, read by eye from the wiring pages of Suzuki's manuals
(owner-supplied 2026-11-26). Medium confidence; pages are not stored. usage: python3 scripts/knowledge/wiring9.py"""
import sys,os
sys.path.insert(0,os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)),'pre2020'))
from _lib import File
F=File('wiring9_suzuki','w-s2','Suzuki 2017 RM-Z250 and 2022 RM85 wiring (wiring pass 2026-11)','Suzuki',['RM-Z250','RM85'],[2017,2022])
s=F.src('manufacturer',"Suzuki RM-Z250 2017 owner's service manual, wiring diagram page 5-9",'https://www.suzukicycles.com','2016')
F.R('ecu_electronics','Harness wire colours at every component',['RM-Z250'],[2017],
 "Main-harness wire colours at each plug on the 2017 RM-Z250. Magneto: yellow, yellow (charging) plus green/white and blue (pickup). Regulator/rectifier: yellow, yellow, red, black/white. Condenser: red and black/white. Fuel pump: red/black and red. Injector: gray/white and red. Ignition coil: white/blue and black/white. Engine stop switch: black/yellow and black/white. Throttle position sensor: red/blue, yellow, black/brown. Intake air pressure sensor: red/blue, green/black, black/brown. Intake air temperature sensor: dark green and black/brown. Coolant temperature sensor: black/blue and black/brown. Tip-over sensor: red/blue, brown/white, black/brown. Gear position switch: blue/black, pink, black/white. S-HAC (launch) switch: red, blue/red, white/red, black/white. Optional battery lead: red and black/white. Red/blue is common to the throttle, intake pressure and tip-over sensors, black/brown is the shared sensor return, and black/white is the frame ground. Some parts have a short pigtail in different colours, so read the harness side of the plug. Suzuki's letters: B black, Bl blue, Br brown, Dg dark green, G green, Gr gray, Lg light green, O orange, P pink, R red, W white, Y yellow.",
 {'magneto':'Y, Y, G/W, Bl','regulator_rectifier':'Y, Y, R, B/W','condenser':'R, B/W','fuel_pump':'R/B, R','injector':'Gr/W, R','ignition_coil':'W/Bl, B/W','stop_switch':'B/Y, B/W','tps':'R/Bl, Y, B/Br','iap':'R/Bl, G/B, B/Br','iat':'Dg, B/Br','ect':'B/Bl, B/Br','tip_over':'R/Bl, Br/W, B/Br','gear_position':'Bl/B, P, B/W','s_hac_switch':'R, Bl/R, W/R, B/W'},'OEM',s,'medium','Read from the wiring diagram by eye; check the diagram on the bike before cutting, splicing or back-probing.')
s2=F.src('manufacturer',"Suzuki RM85 2022 owner's service manual, electrical circuit page 13-2",'https://www.suzukicycles.com','2021')
F.R('ecu_electronics','Complete ignition wiring',['RM85'],[2022],
 "The 2022 RM85 has no battery and one small circuit. The magneto feeds the CDI unit on three wires: black/red, red/white and black/white. The CDI fires the ignition coil on white/blue, and black/white is the ground shared by the CDI and the coil. The engine stop switch is on black/yellow from the CDI and grounds it to the frame when pressed. Suzuki's colour code: B/W black with white tracer, B/R black with red tracer, R/W red with white tracer, B/Y black with yellow tracer, W/Bl white with blue tracer.",
 {'magneto_to_cdi':'B/R, R/W, B/W','cdi_to_coil':'W/Bl','ground':'B/W','stop_switch':'B/Y to ground'},'OEM',s2,'medium','Read from the circuit drawing by eye.')
F.write()
